  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed use does not constitute development requiring planning permission under Section 55 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended). The Applicant has demonstrated that the operation described in the application would be ancillary to the main lawful use of the premises as a place of worship (Use Class F1(f)), and therefore would not give rise to a material change of use.",
    "Notwithstanding the submitted plans and supporting information, this Certificate relates solely to the proposed use of part of the building as an ancillary community refreshment space. It does not grant or imply consent for any external alterations or operational development, including the installation of new windows or other external works, which would require separate planning permission.",
    "For the avoidance of doubt, should the approved ancillary community refreshment space evolve into a separately operated or commercial enterprise open to the general public, or otherwise cease to be ancillary to the lawful use of the premises as a place of worship, this may constitute a material change of use for which planning permission would be required."
  ],
